From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: expand the strongest peaks when peak_count exceeds HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH

hx_detect_peaks() sorts detected peaks in ascending order of signal strength,
but hx_expand_and_resolve() previously iterated from index 0 and stopped after
HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH (10) peaks, dropping the strongest peaks whenever palm fragments
pushed peak_count above 10.

Start peak expansion at max(0, peak_count - HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH) so the weakest
peaks are skipped and the strongest HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH peaks are expanded.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
index acbcd6ac0..0d2b8dbb1 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
@@ -996,9 +996,16 @@ void hx_expand_and_resolve(struct hx_algo *algo,
 	memset(algo->zone_map, 0, sizeof(algo->zone_map));
 	algo->contact_count = 0;
 
-	n = min_t(int, algo->peak_count, HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH);
+	/*
+	 * peaks[] is sorted ascending, so with more peaks than slots the
+	 * strongest are the last ones.  Taking the first HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH
+	 * dropped exactly those; skip the weakest instead and keep the
+	 * ascending expansion order among the rest.
+	 */
+	n = algo->peak_count;
+	i = n > HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH ? n - HIMAX_MAX_TOUCH : 0;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+	for (; i < n; i++) {
 		struct hx_contact *ct = &algo->contacts[algo->contact_count];
 		bool clean;
 
